WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.599
Monica Rogati who has
moved around a little bit,

00:00:08.599 --> 00:00:11.640
but she's an important data
science leader and writer,

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.279
has the data science
hierarchy of needs

00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:17.039
or the AI hierarchy of needs.

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:21.480
At the bottom are things like
logging and collecting data.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.600
And then you move up and things
at the middle are analytics.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.519
And things like
machine learning are

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:32.399
way at the top of this pyramid.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:35.840
And in terms of value
that people get,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.359
you get a lot of
value from analytics,

00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:41.759
from counting things.

00:00:41.759 --> 00:00:45.240
You get a lot of value
from your first models

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.799
you train, like simple
models, linear models.

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:52.920
It's like you have
to be pretty mature.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.320
You have to be pretty up
to your hierarchy of needs

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.079
to be able to the point
where you're like,

00:00:57.079 --> 00:01:00.200
I need fancy machine
learning model

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.119
that's learning
non-linear relationships

00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:07.640
or taking advantage
of complicated math.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.239
I wouldn't say I'm motivated
to work on machine learning

00:01:10.239 --> 00:01:14.319
because it's the thing
that offers the most value

00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:18.000
or that it's the thing that
solves the most problems.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.560
Because I think the
thing that solves

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:24.000
the most problems is making
data accessible to people

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.719
in their workplaces,
and that they

00:01:25.719 --> 00:01:29.040
have the tools to be able
to do basic analytics

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.599
or train that first model.

00:01:30.599 --> 00:01:35.040
You get the biggest wins
at those lower levels.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.959
I do think the problem is, like,
machine learning tooling is

00:01:40.959 --> 00:01:45.000
interesting because
it is complex

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.760
and people enter into it with
different levels of experience.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:56.879
And being able to
build tools to make

00:01:56.879 --> 00:02:01.840
that process more streamlined
is an interesting challenge.

